## Parallel execution & runtime isolation

Parallelize **branches**, not the same branch (git enforces this). Core rules: worktrees in a sibling `../<repo>-worktrees/<slug>` folder; **feature-based branch names** (never `agent-3-tuesday`); same base commit; lifecycle ≤ 1 day; **max 3–4 concurrent local worktrees**; assign by feature slice, not by file type; clean up with `scripts/worktree-cleanup`. Runtime isolation (Docker per worktree, port offsets, per-worktree `.env`) is **only** introduced when a concrete conflict appears (shared port/DB/services) — never "just in case". Beyond 4 concurrent agents, move to Cursor Cloud Agents / Claude Code SDK in CI.

Full conventions, helper scripts, editor integrations, and the Docker policy: [`references/orchestration.md`](references/orchestration.md).

